{"step_index":104,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T10:30:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T14:30:05+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T14:30:05+04:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/AGENTS.md`\nTotal Lines: 60\nTotal Bytes: 4161\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # AGENTS.md — infra-management-system\n2: \n3: This file provides compact guidance for OpenCode agents working in this Ansible IaC repo.\n4: Every line is something an agent would likely miss without help.\n5: \n6: ## Quickstart\n7: \n8: - **Install deps**: `ansible-galaxy collection install community.crypto community.general` (runner CORP has them pre-installed)\n9: - **Test config**: `ansible-test` fixtures are not set up — run ad-hoc ansible commands locally instead\n10: - **Never run `ansible-playbook` directly on prod hosts** — deployments go through Semaphore\n11: \n12: ## Production safety (RÈGLES DURES — priment sur tout)\n13: \n14: These apply when actions touch prod cluster, inventaire prod, hôtes `trp-*p-*`, runner_tag `PROD`, or Semaphore inventaire prod:\n15: \n16: 1. **Zero downtime.** Only add new (vhost, pool, user). Never reconfigure existing shared instances.\n17: 2. **Reload, never restart.** Use `state: reloaded` for nginx/php-fpm. Never `state: restarted`.\n18: 3. **No file deletion.** Read-only operations only. Exception: `/tmp` scratch space.\n19: 4. **No prod execution without Loïc's explicit approval.** Every `run_task` Semaphore and every command targeting a prod host must be validated coup-by-coup.\n20: 5. **Never trust `dry_run`/`--check`** on the Semaphore runner. Verified 2026-07-24: `run_task(dry_run=true)` applied changes for real on `trp-efaliap-cmp1`. Before any prod-modifying task, first run a read-only reconnaissance playbook (`changed_when: false`, `stat`/`getent`/`getfacl` etc.), read its output, then proceed.\n21: \n22: ## Workflow\n23: \n24: - **1 su\n<truncated 820 bytes>\n - `PROD` → `th2-ansip-run1` (`172.30.199.225`)\n38: \n39: ## Inventory structure\n40: \n41: - **Inventories**: `inventories/{dev,val,prod}/`\n42: - **Hosts** are grouped with explicit children (databases, proxysql, backends, frontaux, batch_retractation_php, proxysql_wm2mp, wm2mp, efalia_compose etc.)\n43: - **Group vars** live in `inventories/{env}/group_vars/` — never edit host_vars to change global config\n44: - **Vault files**: `*_vault.yml` files are never loaded auto-magically — inline `!vault` only in the `group_vars` of the matching group, or the file won't be read\n45: - **Plaintext secrets** `*.SECRETS-PLAINTEXT.yml` are never committed (covered by `.gitignore`) — encrypt to `*_vault.yml` first\n46: \n47: ## Roles & playbooks\n48: \n49: - **Roles**: `roles/` — each is a self-contained Ansible role (nginx, php-fpm, mariadb, proxysql, etc.)\n50: - **Playbooks**: `playbooks/` — the entrypoint is typically `playbooks/base.yml` or task-specific playbooks\n51: - **Check playbooks**: `scripts/check-*.yml` — use these to verify prerequisites before modifying\n52: - **Recon playbooks**: `playbooks/recon-*.yml` — read-only reconnaissance before any prod change\n53: \n54: ## Common gotchas\n55: \n56: - **Git `untracked` pollution**: `git status` stays dirty across branch switches. Always `git stash -u` or commit before switching subjects. Use `git add <explicit paths>`, never `git add -A`.\n57: - **Semaphore `--check` is NOT reliable**: See the production safety rules above — `dry_run` can silently apply changes for real.\n58: - **GitLab corporate SSL**: Always force `openssl` backend (`-c http.sslBackend=openssl`). The corporate cert breaks schannel.\n59: - **Ansible inventory**: `ansible.cfg` sets `inventory = inventories` relative to repo root. Hosts are defined in `inventories/{env}/hosts.yml`.\n60: - **Semaphore runner tags**: Must match exactly. PROD runner is `th2-ansip-run1`. Using wrong tag silently routes to wrong environment.\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
